@startuml wiring_ioc_class_diagram
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName Consolas
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam packageFontStyle italic
skinparam stereotypeFontSize 9
skinparam arrowThickness 1.2
skinparam noteBorderColor #777777

title Wiring IoC - Class Diagram

package "pygim::wiring::detail (common/adapter_validation.h)" as SHARED #F3E5F5 {
    class "adapter validation helpers" as Helpers <<free functions>> #E1BEE7 {
        + ensure_callable(obj, label) : void
        + ensure_callables(objects, label) : void
        + is_instance_of(instance, interface) : bool
        + ensure_instance_matches_interface(instance, interface) : void
    }

    note top of Helpers #F3E5F5
      Shared pybind adapter checks for wiring modules.
      Keeps callable and Python protocol validation out of pybind-free core.
      IoC still owns IoC-only checks such as autowire=True requiring a class.
    end note
}

package "pygim.ioc binding (bindings.cpp)" as BIND #E8F5E9 {
    class "PYBIND11_MODULE(ioc)" as Module <<module>> #C8E6C9 {
        + ServiceDescriptor
        + Container
        --
        + register(..., autowire=False, override=False)
        + resolve(key)
        + describe(key)
        + registered_keys()
    }

    note top of Module #E8F5E9
      Pybind11 exposes the native API as pygim.ioc.
      register() supports direct registration and decorator form.
      The binding does not own lifecycle logic; it forwards to Container.
    end note
}

package "pygim adapter (adapter.h)" as ADAPTER #E3F2FD {
    class InterfaceKeyPolicy #BBDEFB {
        + make_from_python(interface, name) : key_type
    }

    class "InterfaceKeyPolicy::key_type" as KeyType #D6EAF8 {
        + ptr : PyObject*
        + name : optional<string>
    }

    class "InterfaceKeyPolicy::Hash" as KeyHash #D6EAF8 {
        + operator()(key) : size_t
    }

    class "InterfaceKeyPolicy::Eq" as KeyEq #D6EAF8 {
        + operator()(lhs, rhs) : bool
    }

    class Container #BBDEFB {
      - m_core : CoreType
      --
      + register_service(interface, provider, name,
      .. lifecycle, decorators, autowire, override) : void
      + resolve(key) : py::object
      + contains(key) : bool
      + registered_keys() : py::list
      + describe(key) : DescriptorType
      + repr() : string
      --
      - invoke_provider(descriptor) : py::object
      - invoke_autowired_class_provider(provider) : py::object
      - make_key(key) : InterfaceKeyPolicy::key_type
    }

    note right of Container #E3F2FD
      Python-aware adapter around ContainerCore.
      Owns key parsing, lifecycle parsing, decorator invocation,
      opt-in constructor autowiring, and IoC-specific validation.
      Delegates generic callable/protocol checks to shared wiring helpers.
    end note

    note top of InterfaceKeyPolicy #E3F2FD
      Key policy preserves Python interface identity.
      Optional name disambiguates multiple providers for the same interface.
    end note

    note top of KeyType #E3F2FD
      Stores a borrowed PyObject* plus optional name.
      The pointer is used as identity; tuple keys are normalized before lookup.
    end note

    note top of KeyHash #E3F2FD
      Combines interface pointer hash with optional name hash.
      This keeps named and unnamed registrations in the same index map.
    end note

    note top of KeyEq #E3F2FD
      Equality requires both the same interface object identity
      and the same optional registration name.
    end note

}

package "pygim::core (core.h)" as CORE #FFF3E0 {
    enum Lifecycle #FFE0B2 {
        Transient
        Singleton
    }

    class "ServiceDescriptor<Interface,\nProvider, Decorator>" as Descriptor <<template>> #FFE0B2 {
        + interface : Interface
        + provider : Provider
        + lifecycle : Lifecycle
        + name : optional<string>
        + decorators : vector<Decorator>
        + autowire : bool
    }

    class "ContainerCore<Key,\nDescriptor, Instance, Hash, Eq>" as Core <<template>> #FFE0B2 {
        - m_registry : vector<Descriptor>
        - m_index_map : unordered_map<Key, size_t, Hash, Eq>
        - m_singletons : unordered_map<size_t, Instance>
        --
        + reserve(capacity) : void
        + register_or_override(key, descriptor, override) : void
        + contains(key) : bool
        + try_descriptor(key) : const Descriptor*
        + resolve(key, invoke_provider, apply_decorators) : Instance
        + keys() : vector<Key>
        + size() : size_t
    }

    note top of Lifecycle #FFF3E0
      Core lifecycle enum is intentionally tiny.
      transient builds each resolve; singleton caches by descriptor index.
    end note

    note top of Descriptor #FFF3E0
      Immutable-by-convention registration record.
      In this module Interface, Provider, and Decorator are all py::object,
      but the core template stays generic and pybind-free.
    end note

    note bottom of Core #FFF3E0
      Generic registry and lifecycle engine.
      It stores descriptors, maps keys to descriptor indexes,
      invalidates singleton cache on override, and delegates Python calls
      through adapter-provided invoker/decorator callbacks.
    end note
}

Module --> Container : binds
Module --> Descriptor : binds as ServiceDescriptor

Container *-down-> Core : owns m_core
Container --> InterfaceKeyPolicy : build keys
Container --up-> Helpers : validate Python boundary
Container ..> Descriptor : DescriptorType

InterfaceKeyPolicy *-- KeyType
InterfaceKeyPolicy ..> KeyHash
InterfaceKeyPolicy ..> KeyEq

Core *-up- "0..*" Descriptor : m_registry
Core *-up- "0..*" KeyType : m_index_map keys
Core ..> KeyHash : hash policy
Core ..> KeyEq : equality policy
Descriptor --up-> Lifecycle

legend right
|= Color |= Layer |= Responsibility |
|<#E8F5E9> Green | Binding | Public pybind11 module surface |
|<#E3F2FD> Blue | Adapter | Python object parsing, validation, callbacks, autowiring |
|<#FFF3E0> Orange | Core | Generic lifecycle, registry, index, singleton cache |
|<#F3E5F5> Purple | Shared wiring support | Reusable pybind adapter validation helpers |
|<#FFFDE7> Arrow convention | Relationships | Inheritance/realization should point upward from child to parent; usage arrows may route in any direction |
endlegend

@enduml